  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The area of trapezoid \\(ABCD\\) is \\(164\\text{ cm}^2.\\) The altitude is \\(8\\) cm, \\(AB\\) is \\(10\\) cm, and \\(CD\\) is \\(17\\) cm. What is \\(BC,\\) in centimeters?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(15\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "10"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2003-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Drop perpendiculars from \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) to \\(\\overline{AD},\\) meeting it at \\(E\\) and \\(F.\\)\n\nIn the left and right right triangles, \\(AE=\\sqrt{10^2-8^2}=6\\) and \\(FD=\\sqrt{17^2-8^2}=15.\\)\n\nThe two side triangles have areas \\(\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot8=24\\) and \\(\\frac12\\cdot15\\cdot8=60.\\) The middle rectangle has area \\(8\\cdot BC.\\)\n\nThus \\(164=24+60+8BC,\\) so \\(8BC=80\\) and \\(BC=10.\\)\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Drop perpendiculars from \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) to the base.",
        "Use the \\(6-8-10\\) and \\(8-15-17\\) right triangles."
      ],
